[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mThis repo has no linter, formatter, or test runner at all. What should I set up alongside the logger?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mA runner plus a first passing fixture. Redaction and level filtering are pure functions and exactly the kind of logic
[39m  [38;5;246mthat needs tests — a redaction bug is a data leak.[39m
[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m2.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mLint + format (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mESLint + Prettier with standard config. Cheapest to add before any new code exists; keeps the new module consistent.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mBrowser-driven test of the real login page and export flow. Higher setup cost; catches IndexedDB and DOM wiring [39m
  [38;5;246mproblems that unit tests can't.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — just the logger
  [38;5;246mShip the logging subsystem with no new tooling. Fastest, but redaction correctness would rest on manual checking only.
